WEBVTT

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.920
"The First Night"

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.630
Oho.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.510
We got us a pro here!

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.930
Don't let him pick up steam!
Surround and kill him!

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.140
Hi-yah!

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.190
You morons!

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.690
<i>Now </i>who's going to be
surrounded and killed?

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:34.700
Our numbers are pretty damn
different up here on the walls!

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.070
Don't underestimate us!

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.120
We may have been
outnumbered all this time,

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.370
but now the tables have turned!

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.330
And we know how tough
a castle-wall attack is

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:47.040
thanks to our battle at Gaolang Castle!

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.460
As far as we're concerned,

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.720
this castle-defense fight, with the
enemy barely making it up the walls?

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.090
Easiest battleground around!

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.720
Th-They're good!

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.430
Of course! <i>This </i>much they can handle!

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:05.560
The Fei Xin Force really did get here
through hand-to-hand combat.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:10.230
As long as they're here, the main
south wall won't fall that easily!

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.820
His was no half-hearted path.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:18.280
--What's wrong? Fight back!
--For one who began as a servant,

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:22.450
--Stay strong!
--the path he's taken to build up his unit
to where it is now...

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:26.120
It was certainly not a half-hearted one.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.750
I wasn't there at the beginning,
so I haven't seen everything,

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:35.170
but Xin's really been running
along some tremendous paths

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:37.380
to get this far, Zheng.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.350
That's what's made him so strong.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.600
It's all yours, Long Chuan!

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.560
Got it!

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.480
Onto the next one, gang!

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.860
What's this? Our foothold's
been crushed already?

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.360
There's this unit--the Fei Xin Force.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.490
They're the linchpin of the south wall.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:58.910
Oh, <i>them</i>.

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:01.990
With the commander who slayed Lun Hu,
right-hand man to Lian Po,

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.120
formerly of the Three Greats.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.540
Was that him, making all that noise?

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.420
Now get climbin' already, damn you!

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.540
Yep.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:11.670
Huh!

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:15.050
Then maybe <i>I'll </i>just pop over
and take him out!

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:16.380
Not so fast, idiot.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:23.140
Didn't Li Mu order you not to
make an appearance just yet?

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:26.350
Yeah, but they'll just gain
momentum if we do nothing.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:27.890
Especially the civilian troops.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:29.980
It doesn't matter.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:34.520
"Qin"

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:34.520
This south wall isn't even
our target for attack.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:09.740
"Zui Castle - East Wall"

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.040
Bi, sir, the enemy keeps
setting up more ladders!

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.790
The east wall seems to
be struggling, Meng Yi!

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.210
They're harnessing the wind.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.260
The wind?

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.090
I noticed when I was climbing up here:

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:26.510
there's an easterly wind
blowing now and then.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:30.020
Having concentrated so many
of his troops in the east,

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.350
Li Mu must have noticed it, too.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:34.940
Our height advantage in an arrow fight

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.980
is canceled out when
we're firing into the wind.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.450
If the wind is strong enough, it may
even work in the enemy's favor.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:44.490
Bi...

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:47.410
On the other hand, then,

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.910
on Lord Changwen's west wall...

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:55.290
They should be upwind--
and enjoying the upper hand.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.670
That's right.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:00.000
Jie Yi's in the back, on the north wall.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.970
He, ah, seems to have brought
a strange weapon with him.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.890
So our problem now is really...

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:09.970
...the east wall.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:15.730
Bring in more archers!

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:19.980
All that cheering at the east wall...
Are they all right?

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.520
H-He Liao Diao!

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:25.820
Their commander, this Bi fellow--
he's plenty capable, right?

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:29.870
I don't know.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:30.990
What?!

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:35.120
I-I <i>don't</i>, okay?
We've never fought together!

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:40.630
But Bi's a commander
with a solid track record.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:45.010
Since I haven't seen it myself, though,
there's just that sliver of unease.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:49.220
And because of that unease, I came up
with something for the east wall.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:50.760
Keep on firing!

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:53.850
They've raised another ladder!

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:57.690
"Li Mu Army Adjutant"
"Jin Chengchang"

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.520
That's right--don't hold back!

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:06.030
Teach those Qin imbeciles
the true terror of war!

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.660
The enemy's foothold is growing!

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:12.870
I-If this keeps up...

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:13.950
Bi, sir!

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:20.000
Th-The cheers are even louder now!

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.750
He Liao Diao, what exactly
did you <i>do </i>to the east wall?

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.010
It's who I posted there.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.140
I put the most militarily
powerful unit in this castle

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.720
on the east wall.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:33.260
N-Now!

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:36.810
Dispatch our reserves
to the enemy's footholds!

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:37.810
Sir!

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:44.270
Outta the way, civilian troops!

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:50.450
Still feeling deep anguish and intense
fury from having lost their lord:

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:52.370
Raise the flags!

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:53.830
"Biao"

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:57.250
Lord Biao's troops!

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:59.500
How dare you slay Lord Biao!

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.580
How <i>dare </i>you?!

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:01.540
This is for him!

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:02.540
Payback time!

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:03.710
Revenge for Lord Biao!

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:05.670
Every last man here...

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:07.380
...we'll <i>annihilate </i>you!

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:11.510
That's one foothold destroyed already!

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:14.140
And that one over there, too--look!

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:16.010
Exactly as planned...

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:18.140
Bi.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:22.810
The outstanding might of Lord Biao's
soldiers is a priceless weapon

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:25.230
in this civilian army.

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:27.360
So rather than putting
them front and center,

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:31.200
they'll be our reserves who'll
rush the enemy's footholds.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:35.240
We can make the most
of their strength that way.

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:39.410
Though that's not the only reason...

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:44.500
Honestly, I think this castle-defense
fight'll be rough if all we do is defend.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:51.300
I'd like to do something to chip away
at their offense, even as we defend.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:56.970
That'll be a blow to Li Mu's army--
they can't easily replenish their troops.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:08:00.180
The south and east walls
will accomplish that.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:04.100
If they send a lot of
troops up these walls,

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:06.520
we cut them off all at once,

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:10.110
thus gradually thinning their ranks.

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:13.410
What's wrong, Zhao? Is that all you got?

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:17.950
They did it! Nearly every foothold
has been destroyed!

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:20.750
As expected from your strategy, Bi, sir!

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:23.080
Lord Biao soldiers, stand down!

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.580
Return to your castle-wall
defensive positions!

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:27.840
Sir!

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:29.380
I get it:

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:34.010
Lord Biao's troops as a reserve unit,
with them on offense.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:37.720
A hunting ground,
in the midst of our defending.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:42.350
Which means there'll be that many
more civilians on general defense--

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:43.640
and greater sacrifice.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:48.770
You really have grown strong,
He Liao Diao.

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:51.190
Woof woof! Arf arf!

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:53.610
All that yelping from Lord Biao's men.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.610
Oh, such loyal dogs!

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:57.530
Not only were they tough to begin with,

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:01.200
but now they've lost their beloved master.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.460
This'll be a tough one.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:06.460
Send in <i>our </i>elite squad, too.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:07.500
Sir!

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:13.260
Now we'll stain the east wall red
with the blood of <i>both </i>armies.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:14.630
"Xianyang"

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:16.510
Wh-What?!

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:21.680
The King's speech got Zui's 30,000
residents to join the fight?

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:22.680
Yes!

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.730
Yes! Yes!

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:29.360
I-I knew His Majesty could do it!

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.730
To think our King...

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:32.690
...had such power!

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:35.570
So you pulled it off, Ying Zheng.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.990
And the battle situation?

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:44.000
Yes, sir. Fighting is underway at Zui.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.370
They're being attacked on all four sides,

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:49.290
but I've received word that
they're currently holding strong!

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:57.340
With an inexperienced army of civilians,
the first day must be key.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:58.390
Correct, High Commander?

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:03.140
Exactly right.

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:09.520
The tacticians' discretion is crucial
to making it through that first day,

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.020
but what it really comes down to

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:16.280
is the extent to which each and every
one of these civilians can fight.

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:19.410
And that, essentially, hinges upon

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:24.740
the strength of the flames that
His Majesty stoked within them.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:30.670
Zui may yet see the light--
if they can but last this first day.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:36.130
"Zhao"

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:39.300
Come <i>on</i>. This is taking too long.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:41.300
And that's an understatement!

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.060
Diao.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:46.270
What is it, Zheng?

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:49.020
This was one of our hurdles--
this first day?

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:50.730
Yeah.

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:52.310
Look:

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:53.770
The sun is setting.

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:54.770
Uh-huh.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:07.700
Fall back!

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:09.830
--Prepare to set up camp!
--Bring the dead and wounded with you!

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:12.790
Gather up all the gear you can!

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:16.550
We-- We did it!

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:19.220
Tch.

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:25.680
Amateurs--getting all worked up just
because you lasted a single day.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:26.930
That said...

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:31.390
We did it, Xin!

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:34.610
Oh, Lieutenant Chu Shui!
Nice work out there!

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:39.820
Dontcha think there was
somethin' missing, Chu Shui?

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:41.740
On Li Mu's side, I mean.

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:47.240
No. Li Mu's army is a detached force
that's been operating in secret;

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:51.160
they don't have castle-storming
equipment like siege towers.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:54.540
Attack a castle with
simple ladders and arrows

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:58.630
and this is about what you'd get,
Li Mu's army or no.

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:03.430
Besides, the damage we've
taken is hardly insignificant.

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:07.140
I understand the east wall
was particularly hard-hit.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:10.060
And their withdrawal before sunset--

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:14.980
perhaps that's only natural,
with all those troops setting up camp.

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:16.020
Well, whatever.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:19.570
No matter what Li Mu's next move'll be,

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:22.240
all <i>we </i>gotta do is kill
whoever makes it up here!

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:31.410
"Hangu Pass, That Same Hour"
Meanwhile, ever since
Li Mu had gone missing,

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:34.790
the fight at Hangu Pass
had come to a standstill.

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:36.630
Wh-What's this?!

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:40.210
Zui is fighting Li Mu's army?

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:42.470
Where did they get their troops?

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:45.340
I wasn't given any details.

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:46.590
The High Commander asks

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:51.680
that we continue to focus
on defending Hangu Pass!

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:58.940
The coalition army ceased all
movement, watching carefully

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:03.320
for the Qin army at Hangu Pass
to try to return to Xianyang.

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:07.780
In short, both armies were
keeping watch from afar

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:10.040
for any movement from
Li Mu's army or Xianyang.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:17.080
You called it off?

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.500
Yes.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:22.760
The civilian soldiers
fought better than expected.

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:27.430
It would be unwise to use force to beat
them into submission on the first day,

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:30.220
so I changed tactics midway.

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:35.190
At any rate, we'll have Xianyang
to contend with soon enough.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:37.600
So you kept casualties to a minimum, then.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:42.900
Weren't your troops going
pretty hard at the east wall?

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:45.650
--"Our elite squad" and all that--
--Not at all.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:48.870
And <i>you </i>ought to wait your turn.

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.830
It's fine.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:54.250
We can't slay great veterans
like Lord Biao's troops

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:57.620
without shedding some blood of our own.

00:13:57.620 --> 00:13:59.710
But the civilian troops are different?

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:01.460
Of course they are.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:05.300
Even with high morale,
amateurs are just that: amateurs.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:09.010
Given their lack of battle experience,

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:13.180
we will conquer Zui with half our might.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:14.810
Half?

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:16.390
Li Mu...

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:19.150
But... <i>how</i>, exactly?

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:25.490
For now, split each of the four armies
into two neat halves: front and back.

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:27.570
Front and back?

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:30.410
First thing tomorrow?

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.830
No--

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.330
right now.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:43.000
The enemy! Enemy attack!

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:53.720
--That cheering!
--What's going on?
--An enemy attack?

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:55.970
All troops, return to your posts!

00:14:57.770 --> 00:15:01.730
Dammit! A night attack?
And just when we'd caught our breath!

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:04.020
--Xin!
--It's all right!

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:05.900
Diao had her suspicions.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:08.990
We got plenty of troops
on the castle walls!

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:12.120
--Fire!
--Don't panic!
It's no different than daytime!
--Fire those arrows!

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.990
So they <i>did </i>come, Diao!

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:14.990
Uh-huh.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:17.500
How's it look?

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.120
I can't tell.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:24.540
It's pitch-black out there with no moon.
I can barely see anything below.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:26.590
No campfires, either.

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.470
Did they purposely put them out?

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:29.590
Mmm.

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:32.550
So we can't get an idea of their numbers.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.300
That's right.

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:36.930
And that deliberately loud cheering...

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.890
Maybe there's not many of them
out in this darkness.

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:43.360
Once they've convinced us of that,
we let down our guard,

00:15:43.360 --> 00:15:45.690
and they attack us in full force.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:50.070
Then all we can do is watch and wait,

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:52.700
staying as prepared as we were in the day.

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:54.280
Uh-huh.

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:57.290
But for how long?

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:02.750
They're really going for it.
And so loud--damn!

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:06.090
Zui's giving 'em a run
for their money, though!

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:09.920
Get to bed already.
We have an early morning.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:11.090
True, true.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:18.810
In fact, only half of the troops
were part of the night attack;

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:22.520
the other half were sleeping.

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:25.560
Furthermore, half of the attacking troops

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:29.230
were within range of Zui
and firing arrows;

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:33.910
the rest stood around them,
doing nothing but shouting.

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:39.620
Zui was furiously loosing
arrows into that darkness.

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:44.870
And so this night attack,
half just for show...

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:47.790
I trust you'll handle the rest.

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:50.880
Please wake me at sunrise.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:51.920
Sir!

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:54.380
...would continue throughout the night.

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:03.640
--Archers, cease fire!
--Archers, cease fire!

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:06.350
S-So few enemies!

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:08.060
But what about the cheering?

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:09.270
What's going on?

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:10.860
We were set up.

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:16.740
Damn--I overthought this.
But we were up against Li Mu!

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:18.620
This is bad.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:21.490
Have everyone inside the castle rest, now!

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:23.790
We still have some time before sunrise.

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:26.290
Just let them sleep--if only a little!

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:32.170
Are... are they seriously
not going to attack?

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.340
Maybe while we're sleeping...

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:42.770
It's morning.

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:43.770
Damn it all!

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:47.440
They're swapping out their troops!

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:49.690
At sunrise--I knew it.

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:50.770
Enemy incoming!

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:52.400
Archers, get ready!

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:55.530
Man, I slept <i>great</i>!

00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:58.870
Wow, Zui looks awfully sleepy.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:03.080
Now, then--let's pick up
where we left off!

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:06.080
"Day 2"

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:08.290
Fire! Fire!

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:13.210
That's the way! Push 'em back!

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:15.470
Whoa! They're holding strong!

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:18.260
Our civilian troops are
digging in their heels!

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:22.140
Maybe they've gotten used to it--
they're more stable then yesterday!

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:28.020
It's almost noon, Kaine.

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:30.150
It is. Strange.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:34.400
They're fighting as fiercely as
yesterday, even on no sleep.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:35.860
Are they, though?

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:39.530
They look about one pinprick
away from exploding to me.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:45.500
And that one pinprick? That's us.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:47.040
Move out, Fu Di Force!

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:49.620
You too, Kaine Force!

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:51.130
All right!

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:53.550
Fei Xin Force, here we come.

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:55.710
Fu Di's and Kaine's units are on the move!

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:02.350
Long Chuan! Can you take
the troops on the right?

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:03.760
You got it!

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:08.690
That's squadron commander
Long Chuan of the Fei Xin Force!

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:11.060
A squadron commander--here, to help <i>us</i>!

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:14.860
<i>You're </i>a big 'un.

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:19.360
And bam: a squadron
commander's head. Nice!

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:22.870
He's <i>fast</i>!

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:26.120
Too slow!

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:27.120
Long Chuan!

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:36.760
Commander Long Chuan!

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:38.880
Lon--Long Chuan?!

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:41.590
Kaine and her unit can take this spot.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:43.600
We'll head to the left.

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:44.720
The left?

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:48.680
That's where <i>he </i>is:
Xin of the Fei Xin Force.

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:51.940
Xi-Xin!

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:53.400
What's up, Yuan?

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:56.900
At Tian Yǒu's...
no, is that Long Chuan's post?

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:59.530
Anyway, something's happened!

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:00.820
Say <i>what</i>?

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:04.240
Like I <i>said</i>...

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:06.490
...you're too slow.

00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:08.790
--Commander Tian Yǒu!
--Tian Yǒu, sir!

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:12.290
Goodness, is <i>he </i>a squadron commander, too?

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:16.800
So Zui's lost <i>two </i>of
their precious tacticians!

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:18.340
Hold up, runt!

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:20.630
I'm not dead yet!

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:23.220
Huh! You're one tenacious old fart.

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:26.010
I'll just be slicing off
that head of yours now.

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:31.640
Hup! What the--

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:33.560
Well, <i>this </i>one's quick.

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.860
Hey, if it isn't Xin!

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:41.190
Over here!

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:43.150
Quit screwin' with me!

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:44.160
Oop!

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:54.250
Heh.

00:20:57.920 --> 00:20:58.880
So persistent!

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:00.380
Xin!

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:03.300
Never mind me! Stop his underlings!

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:07.050
What the hell is up
with his insane speed?!

00:21:07.050 --> 00:21:10.520
Xin can't even graze him with his sword!

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:12.850
Maybe I expected too much from you--

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:17.230
from the man who slayed Lun Hu
of Lian Po's Big Four.

00:21:17.230 --> 00:21:18.570
Lun Hu...

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:22.320
Ooh, I guess that means
I've blown <i>way </i>past Lun Hu--

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:25.200
and me at barely 20 years old!

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:26.740
Cut the crap!

00:21:26.740 --> 00:21:30.240
Lun Hu would put your ass to <i>shame</i>!

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:33.830
Temper, temper.

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:37.290
I'm not particularly hung up
on all that myself.

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:41.550
I was never interested in Lian Po's
right-hand man to begin with.

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:43.380
Because I, Fu Di,

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:47.970
will one day claim the final
spot in the Three Greats!

00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:51.310
Th-The Three Greats?

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:52.850
<i>Him</i>?

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:56.480
And so, Xin...

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:59.440
You ran into the wrong guy. Just give up.

00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:04.110
Did Fu Di go to the left?

00:22:04.110 --> 00:22:06.990
Yes--said he was after Xin
of the Fei Xin Force.

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:11.030
He foisted this spot off on us,
said we could take it!

00:22:11.030 --> 00:22:14.040
Give me a break.
"We could take it," my eye!

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:16.870
This isn't some game we're playing!

00:22:16.870 --> 00:22:21.130
Fine. We'll build a solid foothold here.

00:22:21.130 --> 00:22:24.050
Then we'll take the south wall in one go!

00:22:28.680 --> 00:22:30.550
They're coming after this position!

00:22:30.550 --> 00:22:33.520
Pull back the archers
and stock up on infantry!

00:22:33.520 --> 00:22:35.930
Form a line of shields--tighten it all up!

00:22:35.930 --> 00:22:39.650
Th-The tactician lady?
What're you doing down here?

00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:41.190
Thank the heavens you're here!

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:44.610
Long Chuan's been slain--
we don't know what to do!

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:47.530
I saw. That's why I'm here!

00:22:47.530 --> 00:22:51.990
Keep on pushing! It only takes
one breach to lose all control!

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.540
He Liao Diao...

00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:00.790
Enough's--

00:23:02.670 --> 00:23:04.960
This guy is <i>way </i>hard to handle.

00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:06.460
He ain't that strong, exactly...

00:23:06.460 --> 00:23:09.470
But he moves so fast,
I can't hardly get at him!

00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:15.100
Hell, he might even be a match for
Qiang Lei when it comes to speed!

00:23:18.350 --> 00:23:19.440
Qiang Lei...

00:24:54.320 --> 00:24:58.120
Next on <i>Kingdom</i>: "A Secret Revealed."
